From: SP11 audio reverse-engineering <sp11-audio@local>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 19:41:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: lpass-tx-macro: SP11 order VA DMIC before rate

The Windows EP16 qcaucd register oracle programs both TX DMIC selectors,
then acquires the shared VA DMIC clock, and only afterwards programs TX
path rate/clock state.

Linux ASoC calls the TX codec DAI hw_params callback before DAPM powers the
DEC widgets. Patch 0078 originally acquired the VA resource from DEC
POST_PMU, so tx_macro_hw_params() could write CDC_TXn_PCM_RATE first.

A fail-closed SP11 diagnostic returned -EAGAIN immediately before those
rate writes. The same snd_pcm_hw_params() call then completed without the
hard reset seen when the writes were allowed, localizing the first unsafe
boundary to this ordering inversion.

For the exact Denali EP16 AIF1 DEC0+DEC1 route, acquire the VA-owned DMIC
resource before programming TX PCM rate. The existing POST_PMU request is
idempotent once the resource is active, and POST_PMD remains the measured
Windows release point.

Signed-off-by: SP11 audio reverse-engineering <sp11-audio@local>
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
@@ -1225,6 +1225,25 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * ASoC calls the codec DAI hw_params callback before powering the DAPM
+	 * DEC widgets.  Windows does the opposite dependency ordering for EP16:
+	 * both TX lane selectors are established, then VA enables the shared
+	 * DMIC clock, and only then does TX program its path rate/clock state.
+	 * Acquire the VA-owned resource here so the following rate writes cannot
+	 * precede it.  The POST_PMU request is intentionally idempotent and the
+	 * existing POST_PMD path remains the Windows-matched release boundary.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali") &&
+	    dai->id == TX_MACRO_AIF1_CAP &&
+	    tx->active_ch_mask[dai->id] == (BIT(TX_MACRO_DEC0) | BIT(TX_MACRO_DEC1))) {
+		int ret;
+
+		ret = tx_macro_sp11_va_dmic_request(component, true);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	for_each_set_bit(decimator, &tx->active_ch_mask[dai->id], TX_MACRO_DEC_MAX)
 		snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, CDC_TXn_TX_PATH_CTL(decimator),
 					      CDC_TXn_PCM_RATE_MASK,
